<!--
================================================================================
  putComposition (Referral Notes) — Sample XML for Referral Memorandum
  Project:    NEHR Onboarding — Heart Clinic / MDXcess GCMS
  Spec ref:   putComposition_v0.2_(RefNotes)_20251224.xlsx (Synapxe), Request tab
  Generated:  2026-07-07

  SCENARIO
  =================
  Mr TAN AH BENG (71 y/o male, NRIC S5512345A) — the same continuity patient
  used in the medication and allergy samples (AF + HTN). At his 2026-07-07
  review, Dr Ruth Kam (MCR 04173D) decides his paroxysmal AF is inadequately
  rate-controlled on medication and refers him to National Heart Centre
  Singapore for electrophysiology assessment / catheter ablation.

  DOCUMENT MODEL (differs from the six "flat" interfaces)
  =================
  putComposition is a DOCUMENT interface like putCardiology:
    controlHeader > patient > composition
    composition = metadata (type/title/status/creator/author/custodian/encounter)
                  + repeating <section> blocks.
  Each <section> carries exactly ONE <content>, and the content holds ONE kind
  of payload:
    - <referralRequest>  : the structured referral (status, type, specialty,
                           requester, recipient, reason). Section TITLE MUST BE
                           OMITTED for this section (spec, Request tab row 133).
    - <other>            : label/value "notesItem" pairs (code 1) or a base64
                           fileAttachment (code 2), for the free-text sections
                           (Patient / Clinician / Referral Information).

  !! SPELLING IS INTENTIONAL: <practitoner> (sic) inside referralRequest
     requester/recipient. Spec: "Keeping 'practitoner' name to avoid breaking
     existing systems." DO NOT correct it — XSD validation will fail.

  OPEN ITEMS (SPOC)
  =================
  1. Multiple <other> blocks per content: spec says each notesItem carries ONE
     name+text pair and NEHR renders it as a single line item, so a section
     like "Patient Information" needs several <other> blocks. Cardinality
     (other 0..*) supports this — confirm reading with SPOC.
  2. Service_Specialty_(NEHR) code for Cardiology assumed "NEHR_SS_0002" from
     the spec's sample value — verify against the actual code-set file.
  3. GCMS today stores referrals as FREE TEXT. Structured fields below marked
     [GCMS-NEW] require the Windows-program schema/UI work (see dev task list NEHR_GCMS_StructuredData_Dev_Tasks_2026Jul07.md). ================================================================================
-->
<putComposition>

